## 3. Government Data Access — How Zona Works

This section explains in detail how Zona accesses government land records, because we believe transparency about this matters.

### 3.1 Public Records Used by Zona

Zona helps you access publicly available data from official government portals, including:

- **Apnakhata** (https://apnakhata.rajasthan.gov.in/) — Jamabandi and ROR records for Rajasthan
- **Bhunaksha Rajasthan** (https://bhunaksha.rajasthan.gov.in/) — Cadastral maps for Rajasthan
- **Rajdharaa** (https://gis.rajasthan.gov.in/) — GIS boundary data for Rajasthan
- **Web Girdawari** (https://webgirdawari.rajasthan.gov.in/) — Crop and cultivation records
- **Jansoochna** (https://jansoochna.rajasthan.gov.in/) — Public information portal
- **HSAC** (https://hsac.org.in/) — Cadastral data for Haryana
- **Other state government land records portals** as we expand to new states

These records are designated as **public records** under the Rajasthan Land Revenue Act, equivalent state legislation in other states, and the Right to Information Act, 2005. Citizens have a statutory right to access this information.

### 3.2 How the Data Reaches You

For most government data, the data fetch happens **directly between your device and the government portal**. Zona acts as an interface that helps you access information you are already entitled to access. We do not maintain bulk copies of government databases on our servers.

In certain cases, our backend servers fetch and process this data — for example, when generating custom nakshas, performing reverse geocoding, or running market intelligence aggregations for our Dominate product. In these cases, we cache only what is necessary to deliver the requested feature, and we do not redistribute raw government records as bulk data products.

### 3.3 Accuracy and Authenticity

Government records may contain errors, be out of date, or have been recently modified by the issuing authority. Zona displays this information as received from the source, and **we do not certify, verify, or guarantee the accuracy of any government record**. Always verify critical information directly with the relevant government office before making property or financial decisions.

### 3.4 Removal Requests for Land Record Subjects

If you appear in publicly available land records and wish to request that your information be removed from Zona's display layer (note: this does not affect the underlying government records, only Zona's display), please contact our Grievance Officer at **grievance@zonamap.in**. We will evaluate such requests on a case-by-case basis in accordance with the DPDP Act 2023 and applicable law.

